{
  "title": "Madelung's Deformity",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/hand/6070/madelungs-deformity",
  "subtitle": "Updated: Dec 18 2023",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "summary",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Madelung's Deformity is a congenital dyschondrosis of the distal radial physis that leads to partial deficiency of growth of the distal radial physis.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "5",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Diagnosis is made radiographically with disruption of the ulnar volar physis of the distal radius, excessive radial inclination, excessive volar tilt, and ulnar carpal impaction.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Treatment is observation in patients who are asymptomatic. Operative management is indicated for patients with wrist pain, decreased range of motion, and/or functional limitations.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Epidemiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "5",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "occurs predominantly in adolescent females",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "5",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "common in gymnasts",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Etiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Pathophysiology",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "caused by disruption of the **ulnar volar physis of the distal radius**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/6070/images/xray.jpg",
                  "caption": "Plain radiograph of the wrist showing a Madelung&#39;s deformity."
                }
              ],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "repetitive trauma or dysplastic arrest",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "leads",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "-1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "**excessive radial inclination** and **volar tilt**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "**ulnar carpal impaction**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "one hypothesis is due to tethering by **Vickers ligament**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "Vickers ligament is a fibrous band running from the distal radius to the lunate on the volar surface of the wrist (radio-lunate ligament)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "may be accompanied by anomalous palmar radiotriquetral ligament",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Genetics",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**autosomal dominant**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Associated conditions",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**Leri-Weill dyschondrosteosis**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "rare genetic disorder caused by mutation in the SHOX gene",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "SHOX stands for short-statute homeobox-containing gene",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "anatomically at the tip of the sex chromosome",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "causes mesomelic dwarfism (short stature)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "associated Madelung's deformity of the forearm",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Presentation",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Symptoms",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "most are **asymptomatic until adolescence**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "symptoms include",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**symptoms of ulnar impaction**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "**median nerve irritation**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Physical exam",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "leads to **ulnar and volar displacement of hand**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/6070/images/madelungs%20deformity.jpg",
                  "caption": "The right wrist here shows increased ulnar deviation which is seen in Madelung&#39;s deformity."
                },
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/6070/images/madulungs%20deformity.jpg",
                  "caption": "The left wrist shows a Madelung&#39;s deformity with increased volar translation."
                },
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/6070/images/medeulung%20deformity.jpg",
                  "caption": "This photograph shows a patient with bilateral Madelung&#39;s deformity."
                }
              ],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "restricted forearm rotation",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Imaging",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Radiographs",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "can see proximal synostosis",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "characteristic undergrowth of the volar, ulnar corner of the radius",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "increased radial inclination",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "increased volar tilt",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "MRI",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "indications",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "concern for pathologic Vickers ligament",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "views",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "thickening ligament from the distal radius to the lunate",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/6070/images/vickers%20mri.jpg",
                      "caption": "T1 MRI of the wrist showing a thick ligament from the distal radius to the lunate."
                    }
                  ],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Treatment",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Nonoperative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**observation**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "if asymptomatic",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "restricted activity",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "activities with repetitive wrist impaction",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "recommend cessation of weight-bearing activities until pain decreases",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Operative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "physiolysis with release of Vickers ligament",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "wrist pain or decreased range of motion",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "efficacy of prophylactic release of Vickers ligament in mild deformity in skeletally immature patients unknown",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "radial corrective osteomy+/- distal ulnar shortening osteotomy",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "wrist pain or decreased range of motion",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "cosmetic deformity",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "functional limitations",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "DRUJ arthroplasty",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "highly controversial",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "painful DRUJ instability and limited supination/pronation",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "significant deformity may require staged procedures",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Techniques",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "**Physiolysis and release of Vickers ligament**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "approach",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "volar approach to the distal radius",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "technique",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "release a pathologically thick ligament",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "ligament approximately 0.5 to 1.0 cm in diameter",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "bar resection and fat grafting in the physis",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**Corrective radial osteotomy +/- distal ulnar shortening osteotomy**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [
            {
              "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/6070/images/madelungs%20postop.jpg",
              "caption": "A patient after a distal radio-ulnar joint fusion for a Madelung&#39;s deformity and ulnar shortening osteotomy.."
            }
          ],
          "importance": "5",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "goals",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "restore mechanics of distal radius",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "approach",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "volar approach to the distal radius",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "technique",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "severe deformities may benefit from a staged procedure with initial distraction external fixation to avoid neurovascular stretching injury of a single procedure",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "codome osteotomy allows correction of coronal and sagittal deformity",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Complications",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Incomplete physiolysis or premature growth arrest",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Violation of radiocarpal or ulnocarpal joint",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Incomplete deformity correction",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Recurrent deformity",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Nonunion of the osteotomy site",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Continued ulnar impaction (if radial osteotomy done alone)",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
